-- B-7 (P0): bootstrap destination tier — seeds `places` with a
-- pre-populated Overture `divisions`/`division`/`locality` subset so a
-- fresh install can search-and-pick a destination before any on-demand POI
-- ingest has ever run (the cold-start deadlock: trip create requires a
-- spine-backed pick, but the spine was empty until a trip existed).
--
-- Cut: population >= 100,000 OR sovereign-country-capital, Overture release
-- 2026-08-19.0 (pinned — no `latest` alias exists). 6,927 rows, generated by
-- `scripts/generate-destination-tier.ts` from `reference-data/destinations.json`,
-- emitted by `scripts/destination-tier-to-sql.ts` (both reviewer-rerunnable
-- and diffable against this file — same posture as 0002's airports/airlines
-- seed). `source='overture'`, `source_id` = the Overture GERS division id
-- (upsert key `places_source_source_id_uq`), `category='locality'` (derives
-- `coarse_category='other'` on read — no `locality` rule in
-- `COARSE_CATEGORY_RULES`), `wiki_ref` from Wikidata where Overture carries
-- one. `created_by` stays NULL (only required for `source='custom'`).
--
-- A refresh (new Overture release) ships as a NEW migration that
-- deletes+reinserts — never an edit to this file (Law #6), same posture as
-- the airports/airlines refresh path (`reference-data/README.md`).
